DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260611
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Keathley v. Buddy Ayers Construction\, Inc.
DESCRIPTION:PRELIMINARY PRINT \nVolume 608 U. S. Part 2 \nPages 647–667 
 \nOFFICIAL REPORTS \nOF \nTHE SUPREME COURT \nJune 11\, 2026 \nREBECCA A. 
 WOMELDORF \nreporter of decisions \nPage Proof Pending Publication\nNOTICE
 : This preliminary print is subject to formal revision before \nthe bound 
 volume is published. Users are requested to notify the Reporter \nof Decis
 ions\, Supreme Court of the United States\, Washington\, D. C. 20543\, \np
 io@supremecourt.gov\, of any typographical or other formal errors. \nOCTOB
 ER TERM\, 2025 647 \nSyllabus \nKEATHLEY v. BUDDY AYERS CONSTRUCTION\, INC
 . \ncertiorari to the united states court of appeals for \nthe fth circ
 uit \nNo. 25–6. Argued March 24\, 2026—Decided June 11\, 2026 \nThomas
  Keathley and his wife fled a Chapter 13 bankruptcy petition in \nU. S. Ba
 nkruptcy Court in December 2019. The Bankruptcy Code re-\nquires debtors t
 o fle bankruptcy schedules listing their property\, includ-\ning “[c]lai
 ms against third parties\, whether or not [the debtor] ha[s] fled \na laws
 uit or made a demand for payment.” Offcial Form 106A/B\, \nSchedule A/B:
  Property\, Pt. 4\, Question 33. Debtors must swear \n“[u]nder penalty o
 f perjury” that the information provided is “true and \ncorrect.” Of
 fcial Form 106Dec\, Declaration About an Individual Debt-\nor's Schedules.
  In April 2020\, based on the Keathley's disclosures\, the \nBankruptcy Co
 urt confrmed an amended repayment plan providing for \ninterest-free repay
 ment of 100% of creditors' claims over fve years. In \nAugust 2021\, while
  the bankruptcy case remained open\, Keathley was \ninvolved in a car acci
 dent in Mississippi with a driver employed by \nBuddy Ayers Construction\,
  Inc. Keathley retained a personal-injury \nattorney and informed his bank
 ruptcy counsel that he intended to sue \nBuddy Ayers Construction. Neither
  Keathley nor his bankruptcy \ncounsel disclosed the potential personal-in
 jury claim to the Bankruptcy \nCourt. Keathley then fled a personal-injury
  action in U. S. District \nCourt in December 2021\, asserting negligence 
 claims against the c\nhttps://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/608us2r4
 8_k53m.pdf
URL:https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/608us2r48_k53m.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3b4fe914863fed74@role-bankruptcy.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260904T111630Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Updates to the National Pollutant Discharge E
 limination System Definitions and Exclusions
DESCRIPTION:The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) proposes to rev
 ise a regulatory definition under the Clean Water Act (CWA) permitting reg
 ulations pertaining to discharges in the contiguous zone and ocean. The pr
 oposal would revise the regulatory definition of "discharge of a pollutant
 " to reflect and faithfully implement the statutory exclusion of vessels a
 nd other floating craft that add pollutants in the contiguous zone or the 
 ocean from inclusion in the definition of "discharge of a pollutant" or "d
 ischarge"\, and thus\, from National Pollutant Discharge Elimination Syste
 m (NPDES) program requirements. The proposed rulemaking would also make co
 nforming and clarifying changes to the NPDES regulatory exclusion for vess
 els and other floating craft. The effect of these changes would be that th
 e addition of pollutants by a vessel or other floating craft in the contig
 uous zone or the ocean that is not secured to the seabed would not be a di
 scharge and would not require CWA NPDES permit authorization to add pollut
 ants to those waters.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/0
 4/2026-18134/updates-to-the-national-pollutant-discharge-elimination-syste
 m-definitions-and-exclusions
URL:https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/09/04/2026-18134/update
 s-to-the-national-pollutant-discharge-elimination-system-definitions-and-e
 xclusions
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
